Template: shepetal/enable-user-service
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Start shepetal automatically when ${user} logs in?
 shepetal runs as a systemd user service (shepetal.service). If you agree,
 it is enabled for ${user} only and starts at the next graphical login.
 Other users can turn it on for themselves with
 "systemctl --user enable --now shepetal.service".

Template: shepetal/service-user
Type: string
Description: for internal use: the user the start-at-login answer belongs to
 The answer to shepetal/enable-user-service applies to this user only.
